1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:26,540
Good morning.

2
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:27,220
Good morning.

3
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:28,880
Hope you all are doing well.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,300
That's wonderful.

5
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,420
So glad.

6
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:40,620
For those of you that I have not had the privilege of meeting, my name is Ryan, and I am one

7
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:41,420
of the pastors here.

8
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:44,980
I am so grateful that you all have made the time to join us.

9
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:47,320
I pray regularly as I come to church.

10
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:53,560
On my way to church, I'm just so thankful for what I call you all my family, my spiritual

11
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:53,960
family.

12
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:59,180
So many of you are such an encouragement to me, and I know I watch you all encourage one

13
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:03,260
another, and I'm so blessed by that, and just grateful to be a part of this community.

14
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:05,440
So thank you.

15
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:10,960
We are entering a new series that we talked about a few months ago.

16
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,900
I asked you for questions that you might have about the Bible.

17
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:17,860
Does anyone remember me asking you for questions about the Bible?

18
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:18,260
Okay.

19
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:25,140
I received over 20 questions about the Bible, which is wonderful, which I won't be able

20
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:26,100
to answer all of them.

21
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:29,400
Some of you that I know I couldn't get to have reached out to you individually.

22
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:31,420
We've had some discussions about some of those.

23
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:35,800
I'm going to do my best, and I'm going to keep the rest of them for future opportunities.

24
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:39,920
And so I just want to make sure we know I'm not going to be able to answer all the questions.

25
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:45,780
But I was honestly kind of shocked by the questions that I received, and shocked in a good way.

26
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:51,960
Because I don't know if I'm like, I don't know, I'm usually an optimist, but for whatever

27
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:59,000
reason, I felt like I was going to get gotcha questions on like hot topic cultural issues.

28
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,920
Like I thought you guys were going to back me into a corner and make me try and weasel

29
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:04,140
myself out of that corner.

30
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:04,620
I don't know.

31
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:08,280
I just talked about how wonderfully encouraging ours is a spiritual family.

32
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:12,480
And then when I asked you to give me questions about the Bible, I assumed that you were going

33
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:15,380
to put me in a corner, and you didn't.

34
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:20,560
I don't know if that's just out of love for your pastor or out of a wantingness, a desire

35
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:23,180
that our church doesn't fall apart in one sermon series.

36
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:27,940
I don't know why you chose not to do that, but I'm so thankful that you did.

37
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:33,700
And I really, I kind of received two different types of questions, which were super encouraging

38
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:34,500
to me as a pastor.

39
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:38,920
The first type of question that I received is like, I received some really base level

40
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:43,880
Christian questions from new believers or people that aren't even yet believers that

41
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:47,420
are kind of following this journey of figuring out who Jesus is.

42
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:50,820
And they asked some really good basic questions about faith.

43
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:55,080
And then another group of people, some of the more mature believers that have been walking

44
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:56,160
with Jesus for a long time.

45
00:02:56,240 --> 00:03:02,780
You all sent me some nuanced theological questions, and you're thinking critically about complex

46
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:05,500
questions, which is awesome.

47
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:06,340
I love that.

48
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:08,560
It encouraged my heart.

49
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:12,780
It solidified for me what I already believe to be true about our church, which is that we

50
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:16,700
are doing church in a way that is accessible for people who are brand new to Christian faith.

51
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:18,040
They can come in.

52
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:20,060
They can follow along with what's happening.

53
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:22,660
They might not always get what we're doing here.

54
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:28,580
But they understand enough that they can follow along and figure out who this Jesus guy is.

55
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:32,280
And they have questions about what it looks like to follow him.

56
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:38,040
And our mature believers, they don't want oversimplified black and white answers to complex questions.

57
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:43,840
Which I've been a part of churches where people would just give me the black and white answer.

58
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:44,820
Just tell me what's right.

59
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:45,560
Tell me what's wrong.

60
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:48,200
Don't give me nuance that's difficult, that's challenging.

61
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,200
I don't want any of that.

62
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:50,380
Just tell, you're the pastor.

63
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:51,960
You tell me what's right and what's wrong.

64
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:59,060
And I love, I love that our church family is a church that is willing to kind of live in the tension

65
00:03:59,060 --> 00:04:00,660
and the nuance of the Scriptures.

66
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:05,920
The Scriptures are tense and nuanced and difficult to understand at times.

67
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:12,120
So that's what we're going to do for the next few weeks is dive into some of those base level questions

68
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:13,820
and nuanced theological questions.

69
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:22,020
And hopefully, my prayer for this whole series is it gives us a much more robust relationship with the Scriptures.

70
00:04:22,820 --> 00:04:27,440
That we have a positive view of what the Scriptures are, what they do for our lives,

71
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:30,840
what they do to invite us into a relationship with God.

72
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:32,140
Does that sound good?

73
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:36,740
All right, well, this week we're not going to answer a question at all.

74
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:40,960
Because that's what I like to do, right?

75
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:44,020
I like to say we're going to do something and then do something different.

76
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:48,640
No, but what we are going to do is we're going to cover what exactly is the Bible.

77
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:53,880
If we're going to approach the Bible to answer our questions, what is the Bible?

78
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,500
Why does it exist?

79
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:59,920
And how are we supposed to use it when we answer questions?

80
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:03,360
When we use the Bible to answer questions, how are we supposed to use it?

81
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:06,140
So I guess we're actually covering three questions in one.

82
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,300
That sounds ambitious.

83
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:10,600
So let's pray and then we'll get started.

84
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:17,820
Father, we are so grateful for your word, both your written word, the Scriptures,

85
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:26,740
and your living word, Jesus Christ, who is the image of the invisible God,

86
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:33,140
taken on flesh to show us what it looks like to truly be human,

87
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:37,040
to truly live in light of your grace and your mercy.

88
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:43,280
God, may we just, may you just deepen our understanding and our reverence and our love

89
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:49,420
for this book that you have preserved for us to know salvation through Jesus.

90
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:51,420
It's in his name I pray.

91
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:52,000
Amen.

92
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,800
All right.

93
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:57,740
Does anybody happen to know what this sucker is?

94
00:05:57,740 --> 00:06:00,220
Yell it out if you know what it is.

95
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:02,840
T, it's a post driver.

96
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:03,280
Okay.

97
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,080
So it's a post driver.

98
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:05,980
That's what it is.

99
00:06:05,980 --> 00:06:07,840
Now, does anyone know why it exists?

100
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:10,200
Why would somebody have created this thing?

101
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:14,100
For driving posts.

102
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:14,600
Yes.

103
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:17,840
Because I don't know if you've ever tried to drive a post before,

104
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:20,600
but if you did not have a T post driver,

105
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:23,120
you would hit your hand.

106
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:23,680
It would hurt.

107
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:29,820
This makes it easier to drive a post than any other thing that you might use to drive a post.

108
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:30,180
Yes?

109
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:32,000
Okay.

110
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,900
Now, you know what it is.

111
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:34,760
You know why it exists.

112
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:38,980
Does anybody, most of you might then infer how to use it?

113
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:41,080
Yeah?

114
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,140
All right.

115
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:43,940
We got a hole.

116
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:45,720
Put it over the T post.

117
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:46,400
We drive it in.

118
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:46,840
Got it?

119
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:48,040
Yeah?

120
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,360
Okay.

121
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:51,240
So what is it?

122
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,480
Why does it exist?

123
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,200
How do we use it?

124
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:58,040
These are the three most important questions when approaching any tool, right?

125
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,880
We need to know what a tool is,

126
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:01,380
why it exists,

127
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:03,540
and how to use it if we're going to use it properly.

128
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:05,980
And that's what the Bible is, right?

129
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:07,020
The Bible is a tool.

130
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:08,440
So if we're going to use it properly,

131
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,580
we need to know what it is,

132
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:10,740
why it exists,

133
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:14,000
and how to use it properly.

134
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:15,560
Because here's the problem.

135
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,600
If you know what a tool is,

136
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:20,660
and you know how to use it,

137
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:22,940
but you don't know why it exists,

138
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:26,500
even when you have a tool, right,

139
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:27,780
it's still difficult to use.

140
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,600
So if you don't know why it exists,

141
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,240
and the work gets difficult,

142
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:32,760
the work gets challenging,

143
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,760
but you don't know why it exists,

144
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:36,780
you might be tempted to give up on the tool

145
00:07:36,780 --> 00:07:38,140
and try and find a different tool

146
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:39,220
that might work better

147
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:41,160
to do the thing that you're doing, right?

148
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:44,320
You've got to understand why the tool exists.

149
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:46,580
And if you know what something is,

150
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:47,420
and why it exists,

151
00:07:47,420 --> 00:07:49,140
but you don't know how to use it,

152
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:53,260
might end up causing a lot of damage along the way.

153
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:55,920
And the reason I use a T-Post driver as an example

154
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:58,400
is because the first time I was ever introduced

155
00:07:58,400 --> 00:07:59,460
to one of these tools,

156
00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:02,980
the one that was handed to me to drive post

157
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:05,800
was severely dented and destroyed

158
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,720
on this kind of top edge.

159
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:10,100
And I looked at the tool,

160
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,500
and I looked at the guy that handed it to me

161
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:12,020
and I was like,

162
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:13,960
what happened here?

163
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,680
And he was like,

164
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:16,180
well, you know,

165
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:17,200
there's a guy at our church.

166
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:20,420
He knew what a T-Post driver was.

167
00:08:20,420 --> 00:08:21,540
He knew why it existed,

168
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:24,700
but he didn't know how to use it.

169
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:28,020
And so he spent an hour and a half

170
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:31,120
trying to drive posts

171
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:33,840
with the T-Post driver upside down.

172
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:37,040
And so now he has blistered fingers

173
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:39,520
and we have a messed up T-Post driver.

174
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:43,160
So I use that as an illustration

175
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:44,580
because I think it's important

176
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:47,860
that we have all three of these questions answered well

177
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,140
when we approach the Bible.

178
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:50,620
What is it?

179
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:52,300
Why does it exist?

180
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:53,220
And how do we use it?

181
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:56,480
And I'm afraid that whether we realize it or not,

182
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:59,060
oftentimes we as Christians have answers,

183
00:08:59,060 --> 00:09:00,440
or even if you're new to the faith,

184
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:02,460
you're questioning Christianity,

185
00:09:02,460 --> 00:09:05,120
you have some presuppositions in your mind

186
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,560
about the answer to those questions.

187
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:10,100
But what I know as a pastor,

188
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:12,380
as I interact with people around the Scriptures,

189
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:14,500
is that our presuppositions are not the same.

190
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:16,900
Depending on your experience,

191
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:19,760
depending on the type of church you went to growing up,

192
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:23,780
or the type of content that you interact with online,

193
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:28,840
the Scriptures are used in some really diverse ways.

194
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:34,000
And people define what the Bible is in some diverse ways

195
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,820
and why it exists and how it is to be used.

196
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:38,380
And so I just want, as a church,

197
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:42,400
I want us to have kind of a groundwork, a foundation.

198
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:43,740
And you might think,

199
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:45,820
okay, shouldn't we have done that like two years ago

200
00:09:45,820 --> 00:09:47,240
when we started church?

201
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:48,100
Right?

202
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:49,540
Yeah, we should have.

203
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:50,220
We should have.

204
00:09:50,220 --> 00:09:50,780
Definitely.

205
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:55,480
But I think what we all come in here

206
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,580
kind of assuming that we all answer those questions

207
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:58,280
the same way.

208
00:09:58,280 --> 00:09:59,160
And the reality is,

209
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:00,760
I've been pastoring the church long enough

210
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:02,200
and I've had enough conversations with you

211
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,140
that that's not the case.

212
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:05,920
We all kind of have different lenses

213
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:07,320
and angles to that question.

214
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:09,460
So I want to answer those three questions today

215
00:10:09,460 --> 00:10:11,280
in hopes that it will set us up

216
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:13,640
for the rest of the series moving forward.

217
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:14,920
That make sense?

218
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:18,980
Okay, so some of this might feel luxury.

219
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:20,520
That's okay.

220
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:22,680
We're just gonna, we're gonna get into it.

221
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:23,780
We're gonna see where the Holy Spirit

222
00:10:23,780 --> 00:10:25,340
tells me to stop being luxury

223
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:26,440
and start being pastoral.

224
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:29,560
And hopefully we get out of here before 1130, okay?

225
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:31,420
All right.

226
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:33,520
If you want to turn in your Bibles

227
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:35,060
to 2 Timothy chapter three,

228
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:37,060
we're gonna get there eventually

229
00:10:37,060 --> 00:10:39,220
after I finish lecturing some.

230
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:42,720
Okay, what is the Bible?

231
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:46,920
What is this thing that we hold in our hands?

232
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:50,040
Well, it is a masterful collection

233
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:52,380
of multiple genres of literature

234
00:10:52,380 --> 00:10:55,540
composed and preserved over thousands of years

235
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:59,200
by the people of ancient Israel and their descendants.

236
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:03,160
Does anybody know how many volumes exist in the Bible?

237
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:08,700
66 books, two volumes.

238
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:09,120
There we go.

239
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:10,500
I was a trick question.

240
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:11,760
I asked it in a difficult way.

241
00:11:11,760 --> 00:11:13,680
We've got two volumes, right?

242
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:14,540
We've got the Old Testament

243
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:15,520
and we've got the New Testament.

244
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:17,780
Those two volumes are made up of 66 books

245
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:20,340
written by 40 different authors.

246
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:23,360
The first volume is the Old Testament

247
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:24,580
and we all know,

248
00:11:24,580 --> 00:11:27,280
everybody in here knows how the Old Testament starts, right?

249
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:29,040
In the beginning,

250
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:32,380
God created the heavens and the earth.

251
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:34,620
This is how the first volume starts.

252
00:11:34,620 --> 00:11:36,920
It is an incredibly beautiful depiction

253
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:39,780
of an infinite God creating a perfect world

254
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:41,860
for humanity to enjoy and manage

255
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:44,320
under his loving rule and reign.

256
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:47,080
And that lasts about how many pages would you say?

257
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:49,920
Less than one page.

258
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:51,520
Less than one page.

259
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:54,140
Does the beautiful, incredible design

260
